<title>USA: Ekco names new CEO, takes $2.7 mln charge.</title>
<headline>Ekco names new CEO, takes $2.7 mln charge.</headline>
<dateline>NASHUA, N.H. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ekco Group Inc said on Thursday that Malcolm Sherman, currently chairman of board, has been named chief executive, effective immediately, adding that it will take a fourth quarter 1996 charge related to the serverance of former CEO Robert Stein.</p>
<p>Ekco said the special charge of about $2.7 million is consistent with Stein's employment agreement.</p>
<p>Stein, who has been CEO since 1986, has resigned his position to pursue other interests.</p>
<p>Sherman was non-executive chairman of Gordon Brothers, a merchant services business.</p>
